# RSpade release tree: byte-fidelity is REQUIRED.
#
# The release inventory (.rspade-release.json) hashes the EXACT bytes of every
# file, and rsx:framework:verify compares a materialized downstream checkout
# against those hashes. If git normalized line endings, a checkout would
# materialize LF where an upstream package (e.g. vendored node_modules shipping
# CRLF) stored CRLF, and every such file would false-flag as tampered. Disable
# all text/eol conversion so the committed blobs and every checkout are byte-for-
# byte identical to the inventoried tree.
#
# git honors .gitattributes per-directory, so this file also governs the vendored
# rspade_project copy of this tree (system/**) and every converted downstream app
# repo automatically - no separate file is needed there.
* -text
